<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marmaduke Grove</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878–1954</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marmaduke Grove was a Chilean air force officer and socialist politician. On 4 June 1932 he led the coup that overthrew President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-esteban-montero">Juan Esteban Montero</a> and proclaimed the Socialist Republic of Chile, which lasted only twelve days before a rival coup exiled him. In 1933 he helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialist-party-of-chile">Socialist Party of Chile</a> and later served as a senator.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marmaduke-grove.jpg" alt="Marmaduke Grove" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cdte._Marmaduke_Grove_.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
